{"files":[{"content":"#include<stdio.h>\n#include<stdlib.h>\n#include<string.h>\n\n/* Maximum size (in char) for neighbors and compute lists */\n#define MAX 100\n#define PARALLEL_THRESHOLD 256\n\ntypedef struct {\n  int id;\n  float value;\n  char neighbors[MAX];\n} Node;\n\n\n/* Reads input, allocates memory, writes graph size and node list. Returns the graph. */\nNode* read_input(char* fname, int *n, char* list) {\n  Node* data = NULL;\n  FILE *fl = NULL;\n\n  if (fname == NULL)\n    fl = stdin;\n  else\n    fl = fopen(fname, \"r\");\n\n  if (fl == NULL) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n  }\n\n  /* header */\n  fscanf(fl, \"%d %[^\\n]\", n, list);\n\n  if (*n > 0) {\n    data = (Node*) malloc ((*n)*sizeof(Node));\n    if(data == NULL){\n      fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n      exit(1);\n    }\n  }\n\n  for(int i = 0; i < *n; i++)\n    fscanf(fl, \"%d %f %[^\\n]\", &data[i].id, &data[i].value, data[i].neighbors);\n\n  fclose(fl);\n  return data;\n}\n\n/* Returns the index of the node with the given id or -1 if not found */\nint find_by_id(Node g[], int id, int size){\n  int i = 0;\n  while((i < size) && g[i].id != id)\n    i++;\n  if(i < size)\n    return i;\n  return -1;\n}\n\n/* Main program - calls read input, computes sums, prints output */\nint main() {\n  char *fileN = NULL;\n  char computelist[MAX];\n  int n = -1;\n  Node* input = NULL;\n  int *successor = NULL;\n  int *pred_count = NULL;\n  int *offset = NULL;\n  int *cursor = NULL;\n  int *predecessors = NULL;\n  int *frontier = NULL;\n  int *next_frontier = NULL;\n  float *cost = NULL;\n\n  input = read_input(fileN, &n, computelist);\n\n  if (n > 0) {\n    successor = (int*) malloc(n * sizeof(int));\n    pred_count = (int*) calloc(n, sizeof(int));\n    offset = (int*) malloc((n + 1) * sizeof(int));\n    cursor = (int*) malloc(n * sizeof(int));\n    predecessors = (int*) malloc(n * sizeof(int));\n    frontier = (int*) malloc(n * sizeof(int));\n    next_frontier = (int*) malloc(n * sizeof(int));\n    cost = (float*) malloc(n * sizeof(float));\n\n    if (successor == NULL || pred_count == NULL || offset == NULL ||\n        cursor == NULL || predecessors == NULL || frontier == NULL ||\n        next_frontier == NULL || cost == NULL) {\n      fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n      exit(1);\n    }\n\n    /* Select the same single best neighbor used by get_costly for each node. */\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) if(n > PARALLEL_THRESHOLD)\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n      char aux[MAX];\n      char *auxptr;\n      char *t;\n      int best_id = -1;\n      int best_index = -1;\n      float max = 0;\n\n      strcpy(aux, input[i].neighbors);\n      t = strtok_r(aux, \" \", &auxptr);\n      while (t != NULL) {\n        int id = atoi(t);\n        int d = find_by_id(input, id, n);\n        if (d >= 0 && max < input[d].value) {\n          max = input[d].value;\n          best_id = id;\n          best_index = d;\n        }\n        t = strtok_r(NULL, \" \", &auxptr);\n      }\n\n      /* The original routine uses -1 as its no-successor sentinel. */\n      successor[i] = (best_id != -1) ? best_index : -1;\n    }\n\n    /* Build reverse edges for the selected-successor graph. */\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)\n      if (successor[i] >= 0)\n        pred_count[successor[i]]++;\n\n    offset[0] = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)\n      offset[i + 1] = offset[i] + pred_count[i];\n\n    memcpy(cursor, offset, n * sizeof(int));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)\n      if (successor[i] >= 0)\n        predecessors[cursor[successor[i]]++] = i;\n\n    /* Evaluate sink-to-source layers; every selected edge is in the input DAG. */\n    int frontier_count = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)\n      if (successor[i] < 0)\n        frontier[frontier_count++] = i;\n\n    int next_count = 0;\n    #pragma omp parallel if(n > PARALLEL_THRESHOLD) shared(frontier, next_frontier, frontier_count, next_count, cost, successor, offset, cursor, predecessors)\n    {\n      while (frontier_count > 0) {\n        #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n        for (int j = 0; j < frontier_count; j++) {\n          int i = frontier[j];\n          float r = input[i].value;\n          if (successor[i] >= 0)\n            r += cost[successor[i]];\n          cost[i] = r;\n        }\n\n        /* Reserve disjoint output ranges before parallel predecessor scattering. */\n        #pragma omp single\n        {\n          int total = 0;\n          for (int j = 0; j < frontier_count; j++) {\n            int i = frontier[j];\n            cursor[j] = total;\n            total += offset[i + 1] - offset[i];\n          }\n          next_count = total;\n        }\n\n        #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n        for (int j = 0; j < frontier_count; j++) {\n          int i = frontier[j];\n          int destination = cursor[j];\n          for (int p = offset[i]; p < offset[i + 1]; p++)\n            next_frontier[destination + p - offset[i]] = predecessors[p];\n        }\n\n        #pragma omp single\n        {\n          int *tmp = frontier;\n          frontier = next_frontier;\n          next_frontier = tmp;\n          frontier_count = next_count;\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  /* Reuse the precomputed result for every requested ID, including repeats. */\n  for(char *c = strtok(computelist, \" \"); c != NULL; c = strtok(NULL, \" \")) {\n    int nd = find_by_id(input, atoi(c), n);\n    float result = (nd >= 0) ? cost[nd] : 0.0f;\n    printf(\"%s: %f\\n\", c, result);\n  }\n\n  free(input);\n  free(successor);\n  free(pred_count);\n  free(offset);\n  free(cursor);\n  free(predecessors);\n  free(frontier);\n  free(next_frontier);\n  free(cost);\n\n  return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/graph.c"}],"hypothesis":"Replacing per-predecessor atomic enqueue operations with a per-layer prefix reservation and parallel scatter may reduce synchronization overhead when many predecessors become ready together, while preserving the computed costs and output.","notes":"The selected-successor graph has at most one outgoing edge per node, so each predecessor belongs to exactly one current frontier node's reverse-edge range. The existing cursor array is reused to reserve non-overlapping scatter ranges. Input format string escapes are retained as valid C source.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Replace atomic capture increments during frontier construction with a serial prefix reservation followed by static parallel scattering into disjoint next-frontier ranges.","Preserve the existing node selection, topological layer evaluation, float addition order, and output formatting."]}